WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.302
This time last year, it was full scale.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.236
There were missiles.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:03.870
There were tanks

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.238
coming down from the north.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.407
There were paratroopers from Russia

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.875
who were landing nearby Kiev.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:12.145
The siege of this city was being started

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.713
this time last year.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.948
Then very quickly,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.583
they pushed them back within weeks.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.652
And now we hear from people that, yes,

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.987
they were terrified back then.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.022
They did not know

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.289
whether their capital

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.358
or their country would be standing.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.194
365 days later. It is.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.095
And today

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.797
we had a press conference

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.232
with President Zelensky,

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.633
and I got to ask him a question

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.534
about how long

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.569
he thought this war would take

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:39.072
Mr.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.340
President, I'm interested

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.043
in the timeline today on the anniversary.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.345
You spoke to your own forces

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.147
and you called for victory

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.082
within this year.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.184
You have heard the Western friends,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.519
your partners talk about

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.320
as long as it takes.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.021
You know that

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.289
the Russian leader believes

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.391
that time is on his side.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.293
Why do you think that it's possible

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.127
by the end of the year?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.962
And how do you assess

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.598
the meaning of as long as it takes

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.901
from your Ukrainian perspective?

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.136
Do the job losses over time?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.605
Wasn't that your additional watch?

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.607
Thank you for the question.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.408
Indeed.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.310
I want to very much

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.312
If each of us, each partner

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.847
and we in our country,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.949
if we stay as one fist,

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.952
one strong fist and work towards victory.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.955
This is a victory of values.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.623
If they stick to their words,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.891
to their terms,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.227
and it's not just blah, blah, blah,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.728
I believe in it.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.131
We have been partners, strong partners,

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.467
and there is evidence to that.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.602
If we all do our important homework,

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.505
victory will be inevitable.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.640
I am certain there will be victory

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:49.576
if

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.012
so, Brianna.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.582
Last year, the watchword was weapons.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.550
We need weapons to defend ourselves.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.017
This year,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.752
they say it's going to be speed.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.753
We need them quickly

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.921
in order to be able

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.357
to actually launch counter offensives,

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.825
regain territory,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:06.693
and somehow

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.194
get to the bargaining table

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.863
in a position of strength

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.831
so that they can have negotiations

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.899
to end this war

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.100
from a position of strength.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.535
They will not surrender

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.370
and they will not take Russia's terms

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.606
right now, they say. Brianna.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.374
All right, Christiane Amanpour,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.209
live in Kiev. Thank you.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.611
Our correspondents and experts

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:27.380
are standing by with more on this.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.448
I want to start with you,

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.682
General Wesley Clark.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:30.783
In a new article,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.552
you right along with six

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.853
other former NATO supreme

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.522
allied commander, his quote.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.923
Now is the time for America

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.358
and its allies to dig deeper,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.593
to get Ukraine what it needs to win

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.829
and succeed.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.530
And certainly,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.397
this is something we heard

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.632
Christiane talking about that

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.900
the Ukrainians are calling for.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.736
What do America and its allies need to do

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.070
and how could it change the

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.071
outcome of this war?

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:54.207
Well, the

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:54.841
outcome of this

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.342
war is probably going

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.411
to be decided at a negotiation,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.146
but the negotiation outcome

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.181
will be reflecting

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.183
the battlefield conditions.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.918
Ukraine needs

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:07.420
the wherewithal to put Crimea

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.688
under threat.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.455
That means

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.257
getting through the land bridge,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.226
threatening to overrun Crimea.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.494
Putin will come to the table.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.795
But to do that,

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.031
they've asked for 300 to 500 tanks,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.266
another 500 pieces of artillery.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.467
They need fighter aircraft,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.102
they need attack helicopters

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.138
and for whatever reason

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.473
and long range missiles for a reason.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.275
We're not giving them that.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.344
So what we're heading

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:34.380
toward is some kind of a bleeding

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.383
or stalemate in which

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.551
I guess we think we're going

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.019
to get at the bargaining table

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.121
what we didn't get on the battlefield.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.490
And history shows that's unlikely.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.793
Jim, we know that Putin thinks

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.027
time is to his advantage.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.629
He's trying to wait out the West.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.030
Now you have this new intel

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.532
that China is considering

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.567
at least thinking about providing drones

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.069
and ammunition to Russia.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.237
What are you learning?

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.137
Well, the concern is

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.005
and drones

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.707
could be impactful ammunition as well

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.742
because Russia has had trouble

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.744
getting ammunition as it continues.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.512
An intense artillery battle

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.348
really on that eastern front.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.048
Drones as well.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.349
We've seen

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.383
the impact of Iranian

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.719
made drones there in terms of helping

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.354
Russia with its air war

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.356
on civilian targets across the country.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.091
So the biggest concern from the U.S.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.992
and Pentagon

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.760
perspective is that China's

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.995
help will lengthen the war.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.563
It'll give Russia what it needs

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.798
now, particularly what it short of now

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.200
in terms of ammunition.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.402
The other piece of that is more broad,

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.303
and that is that

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.272
you already have a war here

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.806
that is, in fact,

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.942
to some degree a proxy war between

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:36.909
the U.S.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.045
and its allies and Russia.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:40.813
You hear Western officials

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.081
don't want to describe it that way,

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.016
but you have the U.S.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.018
and its allies on one side arming Ukraine

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.319
and you have Russia on the other side.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:46.886
It's invaded

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.889
Ukraine with China deciding to provide

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.658
lethal assistance to Russia.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:51.991
You would

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:52.292
you would

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.860
now have three superpowers,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.427
in effect,

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.396
involved in the largest land war

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.131
in Europe since World War Two.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.565
And that is a prospect

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.534
that speaks to the broader conflict

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.001
going on

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.569
between these superpowers,

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:04.904
really on a number of fronts

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.039
around the globe.

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.007
That could lengthen this conflict

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.143
and also adds a risk of escalation

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.778
beyond the borders of Ukraine.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.211
Caitlin,

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.013
you had a really interesting interview

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.248
with Defense Secretary

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.517
Lloyd Austin about all of this.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.552
Can you tell us what he told you?

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.320
Yeah.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.021
This intelligence that I've talked about,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.890
that China is potentially preparing

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.424
to do this, that

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.858
they're considering doing it.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:26.859
They've cautioned to say that

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.461
they have not made a decision yet.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.129
But it obviously raises the question

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.664
to what Jim was laying out there,

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.433
which is what are the repercussions

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.335
if China does actually take this step

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.736
We know what the consequences would be,

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.371
what it would mean on the battlefield,

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:40.039
but what would it mean for China?

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.040
And this is what Defense

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.175
Secretary Austin told me.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.210
I think China, it

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.145
would be a very, very ill-Advised

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.347
step for China to take.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.915
So would it significantly help

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.717
Russia, though, if they did that?

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:51.050
How much

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:51.751
how much of a blow

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.319
would that be for the Ukrainians

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.087
if Russia starts

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.722
getting that kind of assistance

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:56.823
from China?

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.757
Well, you know, again,

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:58.725
I don't want to

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:01.260
get into hypotheticals, but it's clear

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:01.928
that if

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.363
China has a lot of capability

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.897
in terms of munitions and weapons

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:09.035
and if they they provide the sort of,

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.004
you know, substantial support to Russia,

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.540
it prolongs the conflict.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.208
And obviously,

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.142
that is the concern

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.176
there, that it could

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.811
prolong the conflict in Austin

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.980
told me, Brianna, that he the U.S.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.614
has been delivering

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:22.448
warnings to China,

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.349
basically telling them

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.352
not to provide legal assistance to Russia

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.620
in this battle in Ukraine,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.921
in this war in Ukraine.

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.822
But one thing we should note

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.890
is that Austin himself

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.225
is not delivering those messages

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:33.626
because he's actually not spoken

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.962
to his Chinese counterpart in much.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.797
They tried to speak after the U.S.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.432
downed that Chinese spy balloon.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.401
The Chinese his Chinese counterpart,

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.268
the foreign minister,

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:43.503
did not take that call.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:43.836
And he said

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.705
they actually have not spoken in months.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.240
Something that is obviously concerning

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.708
that the Pentagon

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.143
chief cannot get his counterpart

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:51.511
in China on the phone,

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.212
not for lack of trying

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:53.713
but simply

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.114
because they're not picking up.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.150
Yeah, sour relations indeed there.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:57.817
And Jill,

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.085
Ukraine's head of military

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:02.488
intelligence says that Russia's goal as

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:03.656
they see

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.925
it is to capture all of the Donetsk

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:06.726
and Luhansk,

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.194
Luhansk regions

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.662
by the end of March,

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.964
even if Russia can accomplish that.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.734
Do you think that that would satisfy

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:15.868
Vladimir Putin

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.072
I think you have to ask him,

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:20.606
Brianna,

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.376
what would satisfy Vladimir Putin?

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:25.378
And, you know,

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:28.281
if he really did take Brodsky and then.

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:28.948
Yes,

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.050
and that was kind of the original idea

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.585
that Putin had.

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.320
Maybe you could spin it

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.121
and say, you know,

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.889
we have these regions

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.891
but I somehow doubt that

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.226
that would be the end of it,

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:42.462
because even if they had those,

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.797
I firmly believe they would want

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:45.932
Putin would continue

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:48.734
to want to take over the entire country

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:51.204
or control it in some fashion.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:53.539
Now, that could be

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.541
having a sphere of influence,

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.310
and that was his original idea,

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.179
to take Kiev, decapitate

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.581
the country

00:08:01.581 --> 00:08:03.916
and influence it, take it over.

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:06.452
So I do not believe, sadly,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:07.119
that he's

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.921
going to be satisfied with that.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:09.856
And there are other things

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:10.556
that he can do.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:12.124
If he had those two areas,

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.860
he could try to undermine

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.328
the rest of Ukraine

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.863
or he could create trouble

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:17.997
in the neighborhood.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.065
And that is already

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:20.500
we're looking at Moldova

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.202
and other places where he could do that.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:23.636
Right now,

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.671
General, we're seeing Russia continuing

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.807
to shell across the east in the south.

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.375
The Viognier group claims

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.710
to have taken full control

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.145
of a suburb outside of Bok Moot.

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:34.780
What will you be watching for

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.781
here in the coming weeks?

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.386
So the question is, how

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:41.053
effective will

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:41.721
the Ukrainians

00:08:41.721 --> 00:08:44.824
be moving into the second line of defense

00:08:44.824 --> 00:08:47.360
and inflicting casualties

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.562
and slowing the Russian rate of advance?

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:50.830
So for this

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.232
to work out on the battlefield,

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.434
Brianna, there's got to be a holding

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:56.402
in action.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.303
And Don Bosch

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.171
and the Ukrainians have to be able

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.206
to create

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.173
and maintain

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:01.841
their mobile

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:02.642
strike force

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:04.844
brigades that they'll use to go south.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:06.913
Apparently, that's the plan.

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:09.048
And the Russians want to

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.917
put so much pressure on the Ukrainians

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:12.385
that they can't maintain

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:15.254
the integrity of their offensive force.

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:16.956
So that's what we're watching for.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:19.025
Can the Ukrainians hold and Don Bosch,

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:20.760
can we give them enough ammunition,

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.928
enough artillery?

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:23.729
And then is there going to be enough

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:24.463
left over

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.332
to make that counteroffensive thrust

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.466
toward Crimea

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:28.868
that would bring a successful

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:30.036
negotiation?

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.604
Jim, we're also watching tanks, right?

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:32.939
This first delivery of leopard

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:34.173
tanks from Poland

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:35.541
just arrived in Ukraine.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:37.376
American Abrams tanks

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.612
will take much, much longer,

00:09:39.612 --> 00:09:40.980
according to military officials.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:41.914
Maybe next year,

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:43.516
well into next year even.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:44.717
Is this going to be enough

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:45.952
to make a difference?

00:09:45.952 --> 00:09:47.353
Well, the aim to General Clarke's

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:49.555
point is to give Ukrainian forces

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:50.823
an offensive strike

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:51.991
capability in affected.

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.059
And you've seen this with Bradley

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:53.793
fighting vehicles

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:54.727
that are already going in there,

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.129
as well as European versions of those.

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:57.997
Now, you have

00:09:57.997 --> 00:09:59.732
German made leopard tanks

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:01.400
and Abrams tanks to follow

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.368
to give them the ability

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.603
not just to hold territory,

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:04.837
but to punch through as General

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:05.438
Clark was saying,

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:06.505
those lines to gain back

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:08.307
territory in the East End.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:09.775
They have the ambition as well

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:11.677
of taking back Crimea.

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:13.145
When you speak to Ukrainian officials,

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:14.313
they believe they can do this

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:14.947
and they can do this

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.215
in the coming months.

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:17.617
You had the Ukrainian defense minister

00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:18.517
speaking today

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:19.518
about the possibility

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:20.586
of winning this war,

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:22.622
including taking back Crimea this year.

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:23.856
Now, Ukrainians there,

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.091
they're confident in their abilities

00:10:25.091 --> 00:10:25.858
and they've got a year

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.460
of incredible gains

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.795
in defense to work on.

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:31.263
I would say that U.S.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:33.099
officials at this point are

00:10:33.099 --> 00:10:34.634
I don't say more pessimistic

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:35.868
but perhaps more realistic

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:36.602
about how quickly

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:37.436
they can gain back,

00:10:37.436 --> 00:10:38.971
particularly when you look at Crimea,

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:39.839
given the importance

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:41.340
that Russia places on that.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.274
But these weapons are going

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:44.143
there for a reason, and that is because

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:45.778
it's not just Ukrainian intention,

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:47.346
but also the US US attention

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:48.547
to give them the ability

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:50.049
to take back territory and

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:50.816
not just defend it.

